Enable WebKit's native picture in picture.

WebKit only enables the context menu's "Enter Picture in Picture" when
Settings::allowsPictureInPictureMediaPlayback is on (ContextMenuController
sets shouldEnable from HitTestResult::mediaSupportsPictureInPicture, which
reaches MediaElementSession::allowsPictureInPicture). For WKWebView on macOS
that setting defaults to false, so the item is appended for the video and then
drawn disabled.

Upstreaming note: the same switch would also let Kaset's own picture in
picture button hand off to the system window instead of its floating NSWindow.

--- a/Sources/Kaset/Services/WebKit/WebKitManager.swift
+++ b/Sources/Kaset/Services/WebKit/WebKitManager.swift
@@ -264,6 +264,15 @@
         #endif

         configuration.preferences.isElementFullscreenEnabled = true
+        // WebKit gates the context menu's "Enter Picture in Picture" on
+        // Settings::allowsPictureInPictureMediaPlayback, which WKWebView
+        // defaults to false on macOS. WKWebViewConfiguration exposes the public
+        // switch only under TARGET_OS_IPHONE, so reach the macOS SPI setter
+        // `_setAllowsPictureInPictureMediaPlayback:` through KVC.
+        configuration.preferences.setValue(
+            true,
+            forKey: "allowsPictureInPictureMediaPlayback"
+        )
         configuration.mediaTypesRequiringUserActionForPlayback = []

         // Enable AirPlay for streaming to Apple TV, HomePod, etc.
